    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0945" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2145: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-13T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Supplementing Department’s January 9, 3 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d758-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Two telegrams received today from Tegucigalpa<anchor n="6" xml:id="d758-f2"/>
                    indicating growing concern in Honduras at reported revolutionary activity
                    permitted by Nicaraguan authorities under pretext that they are incidents
                    arising out of the boundary dispute. You are instructed to bring to the
                    attention of the Nicaraguan Government that reports of this nature are being
                    circulated in Honduras and to urge that Government to take the necessary
                    measures to prevent its territory from being used as a base for revolutionary
                    activities against a friendly Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d758-f1" n="5" xml:id="d758-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d758-f2" n="6" xml:id="d758-f2-content">
                <p>Refers to the two telegrams, <hi rendition="#italic">supra:</hi> these were
                    received late on a Saturday, Jan. 10, and were not delivered within the
                    Department until Jan. 12. The Secretary’s telegram was drafted on Jan. 12, but
                    was not sent until Jan. 13.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
